  "source_ref": "pytorch-ff89ebc-cuda-overlay",
  "statement": {
    "body": "The Python decomp of `exponential_` uses `-1/rate * log1p(-rand_like(self))`. When the uniform sample is exactly 1.0 (valid for `curand_uniform` which samples `(0, 1]`), `log1p(-1.0) = log(0) = -inf`, giving `+inf` as the exponential value. Fix: add an epsilon guard \u2014 when `uniform >= 1 - eps/2`, substitute `-eps/2` instead of computing log, matching CUDA's numerical behavior.",
    "labels": [
      "module: decomposition",
      "topic: numerical"
    ],
    "title": "torch._refs.exponential can produce Inf for inputs near 1.0 due to log(0) underflow"
  },
  "task_id": "pytorch__129154__exp_decomp_numerics",
  "version": "v1"
}
